[COMMENTS]
STATION,Velocity area station gauging a natural catchment in the Grampians. Replacement for 15017. GENERAL: Velocity area station, 30m wide. Supersedes Ballinloan (15017) 5km u/s (197 sq.km). Station added to peak flows dataset in August 2021 (WINFAP Files v10). STATION HYDROMETRY: Cableway present. Flows fully contained, gauged to the median annual flood, approx 120 cumecs. The low flow control, a derelict stone weir, is sometimes altered by children. Site prone to ice issues during periods of low temperatures. FLOW RECORD: Dec 2010 flows severely affected by ice and should be treated with caution. FLOW REGIME: Flows are natural.
CATCHMENT,Catchment is in the Grampians (rising up to > 800m) and has steep or moderate slopes. Metamorphic bedrock geology with just over half overlain by superficial deposits. Mainly open moorland with rough grazing; some forestry.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged to QMED.
Pooling Suitability,All flows contained and site is well gauged.
[END]
